WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.180
- [Narrator] So you're at
a New Year's Eve party,

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:05.153
thinking of kissing someone at midnight?

00:00:05.153 --> 00:00:06.707
Let's try some other traditions,

00:00:06.707 --> 00:00:09.581
like the ones involving
snacks, because we get hungry.

00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:11.326
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.326 --> 00:00:12.839
Excuse me, coming through.

00:00:12.839 --> 00:00:14.573
Watch your back.

00:00:14.573 --> 00:00:17.073
Take Spain, where they
eat a grape for every bell

00:00:17.073 --> 00:00:18.491
that strikes at midnight.

00:00:18.491 --> 00:00:20.658
Whoa, slow down Sam, it's just 12.

00:00:20.658 --> 00:00:22.391
Even more delicious?

00:00:22.391 --> 00:00:25.713
Switzerland, they eat whipped cream.

00:00:25.713 --> 00:00:29.567
It's customary to let
some spill on the floor.

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:31.265
If you're looking for
something more healthy,

00:00:31.265 --> 00:00:32.437
look to Chile.

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:34.972
They eat a spoonful of
lentils at midnight.

00:00:34.972 --> 00:00:36.447
Uh yeah, lentils.

00:00:36.447 --> 00:00:38.353
Okay, too healthy.

00:00:38.353 --> 00:00:39.877
How about the Netherlands?

00:00:39.877 --> 00:00:42.992
The dutch eat special sugary doughnuts.

00:00:42.992 --> 00:00:45.421
It's better shared with friends.

00:00:45.421 --> 00:00:48.449
Okay, I know what you're
thinking, where's the booze?

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:51.857
Enter Russia, there it's
customary to write your wishes

00:00:51.857 --> 00:00:53.524
down and burn the paper.

00:00:53.524 --> 00:00:57.003
The ash is then dropped
into some bubbles and drunk.

00:00:57.003 --> 00:00:57.836
Mmm ashy.

00:00:59.071 --> 00:00:59.940
Still hungry?

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.510
In Japan they eat buckwheat
noodles which represent

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.030
longevity and wealth.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.624
Speaking of wealth, if you're
the lucky one to find the coin

00:01:07.624 --> 00:01:09.253
in this traditional Greek bread,

00:01:09.253 --> 00:01:11.388
you're promised good
luck for the next year.

00:01:11.388 --> 00:01:15.098
Yay, looks like Kimberley's
in for a good year.

00:01:15.098 --> 00:01:17.324
But something that's
found around the world,

00:01:17.324 --> 00:01:19.126
good cheer, good friends,

00:01:19.126 --> 00:01:21.744
and maybe a few great big stories.

00:01:21.744 --> 00:01:23.911
[All] One, happy new year!

